{
  "_comment": [
    "Legitimate-publisher corpus for the false-positive measurement.",
    "",
    "Chosen to be hostile to this tool's known weaknesses.",
    "",
    "1. The old detector could only recognise legitimacy through a 63-domain",
    "   allowlist that was overwhelmingly Anglo-American and European. So this",
    "   list is weighted toward the press that allowlist does NOT contain:",
    "   South Asian, African, Middle Eastern, Latin American, South-East Asian",
    "   and European national press, plus independent investigative outlets.",
    "",
    "2. The 'think-tank-unverified' heuristic fires on names containing",
    "   institute, observatory, foundation, forum, watch, monitor. Real research",
    "   institutions are named exactly like that, so the 'Research institute'",
    "   group below exists specifically to catch this heuristic defaming real",
    "   organisations. Every entry there trips the name pattern by design.",
    "",
    "Inclusion criterion is narrow and checkable: a masthead or named staff, and",
    "a multi-year publishing record. It is NOT a claim that any of these is",
    "unbiased or accurate - see docs/SOURCE-LISTS.md."
  ],
